<title>GERMANY: Daimler urges Bonn to decide on Eurofighter.</title>
<headline>Daimler urges Bonn to decide on Eurofighter.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daimler-Benz AG Chairman Juergen Schrempp sharply criticised the German government for delaying a decision on participation in the Eurofighter project.</p>
<p>Speaking at Daimler's annual shareholder meeting, Schrempp said: &quot;I can not understand how one can delay a decision that could have such a lasting impact for German technology.&quot;</p>
<p>Noting that Britain and Spain had already decided on the Eurofighter, Schrempp said that economic benefits meant Germany must quickly make a committment to the Eurofighter.</p>
<p>Bonn has delayed making a decision on the plane because of tight budget finances and internal fighting over who in the government would oversee the project.</p>
<p>--Scott Miller, Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
